    description: "Measured 2026-11-22 on 'hypergumbo run packages --first-party-only' of this repository: the c pass analyses 4 vendored tree-sitter files (vendor/tree-sitter-*/src/parser.c, scanner.c), takes 35-49 s (cpu 35-38 s), emits 42 nodes and 257,091 edges, and none of them is in the output. With '-e vendor' the run takes 262 s against 321 s and the output is identical (same node ids and edge triples). Question to settle: whether a --max-tier / --first-party-only run can skip files that will classify as tier 3 or 4 before analysing them, or whether tier classification needs the analysis (then: why a generated parser.c emits 257k edges in 4 files). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/lutok/RESULTS.md, pass_times.txt."  # 65fe
